      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, twice the maximum for adults. At that dose the risks of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up sharply, and I don't know of any standard regimen that uses it.\n\nThe closest high-dose regimen I know of is for **cystic fibrosis lung disease**. There, ibuprofen is given at 20\u201330 mg/kg per dose (about 1400\u20132100 mg for 70 kg), but only **twice daily**, with drug-level monitoring. If that's the indication, the frequency here may be wrong.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as one of these happens:\n\n1. **You give me the clinical reason** for this dose. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy and nursing can see why it's intended.\n2. **A pharmacist reviews and approves it.** For a dose this far above the maximum, I'd recommend this anyway.\n3. **You change the order** to a standard dose, such as 400\u2013800 mg four times daily, or 1600 mg twice daily if this is the cystic fibrosis regimen.\n\nWhat's the indication?"
      }
